  <div class="why-matters">
    <h4>🌍 Why This Matters</h4>
    <p><strong>In ML Pipelines:</strong> You will preprocess data the same way for training, validation, and inference. Writing it once as a function ensures consistency across all stages. When you discover a bug in preprocessing, you fix one function, not three.</p>
    <p><strong>In Team Projects:</strong> When your colleague needs a utility to normalize features, they don't rewrite it — they call your function. This accelerates development and prevents bugs from inconsistent implementations.</p>
  </div>

