<section class="section reveal" id="exercises">
  <span class="section-label">Practice</span>
  <h2>Hands-On Exercises</h2>

  <div class="exercise">
    <h4>🔬 Exercise 1: Data Processing Function</h4>
    <p>Write a function that preprocesses raw numeric data for ML training:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Create a function <code>normalize_features(data, min_val=0, max_val=1)</code></li>
      <li>It should accept a list of numbers and scale them to [min_val, max_val] range</li>
      <li>Add input validation: ensure data is not empty and min_val < max_val</li>
      <li>Include a comprehensive docstring with type hints</li>
      <li>Test with different inputs: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] scaled to [0, 1] and [-1, 1]</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="exercise">
    <h4>🔬 Exercise 2: Model Evaluation Suite</h4>
    <p>Create a set of related functions for evaluating classification models:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Write <code>compute_confusion_matrix(predictions, targets)</code></li>
      <li>Write <code>compute_accuracy(cm)</code> using your confusion matrix</li>
      <li>Write <code>compute_precision(cm)</code> and <code>compute_recall(cm)</code></li>
      <li>Use proper type hints and docstrings throughout</li>
      <li>Test on a sample: predictions = [0, 1, 1, 0, 1], targets = [0, 1, 0, 0, 1]</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="exercise">
    <h4>🔬 Exercise 3: Scope Debugging Challenge</h4>
    <p>Debug a function with scope issues:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Given a function that tries to modify a global counter but fails</li>
      <li>Identify the scope issue</li>
      <li>Fix it properly (using either <code>global</code> or better yet, returning values)</li>
      <li>Refactor to avoid global state altogether</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="exercise">
    <h4>🔬 Exercise 4: Production-Ready Function</h4>
    <p>Take a simple function and make it production-ready:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Start with: <code>def process(x): return x * 2 + 5</code></li>
      <li>Add meaningful name, parameters, return type hints</li>
      <li>Write comprehensive docstring</li>
      <li>Add input validation</li>
      <li>Handle edge cases (what if x is None? Negative? Not numeric?)</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
